=== act_act2_arc1 ===
# kind: act # key: act2_arc1 # title: ACT II — ARC 1: FRACTURING THE SEGREGATION GRID # subtitle: Levels 5–7: Breaking the Physical Walls of Occupation
The first arc of the mid-campaign focuses entirely on the physical infrastructure of separation—the walls, checkpoints, biometric registries, and behavioral conditioning programs the Xelthara use to keep the human population fractured, surveilled, and too traumatized to organize. Before the resistance can strike at the economic or political heart of the occupation, they must first reconnect the isolated human communities to one another.

-> END

=== act_act2_arc2 ===
# kind: act # key: act2_arc2 # title: ACT II — ARC 2: THE RESOURCE RECLAMATION FRONT # subtitle: Levels 8–11: Cutting Off the Economic Profitability of Colonization
With the Segregation Grid fractured and the isolated populations reconnected, the resistance shifts to the economic engine of the occupation. The Xelthara came to Earth for resources—not ideology. Arc 2 is the campaign of economic disruption: four successive strikes against the extraction, processing, transport, and security infrastructure that makes the occupation financially viable.

-> END

=== act_act2_arc3 ===
# kind: act # key: act2_arc3 # title: ACT II — ARC 3: DISMANTLING CORPORATE GOVERNANCE # subtitle: Levels 12–14: Pushing Into the Heart of the Colonial Administrative State
The extraction engines are halted. The security grid is dark. The segregation walls are fractured. What remains is the administrative and political architecture of the occupation itself. Arc 3 is the campaign's most politically direct sequence: the resistance is no longer fighting an occupying army. It is dismantling a colonial state, piece by piece, from the outside in.

-> END

