=== level_0 ===
# kind: level # level: 0 # title: Protocol Zero - The Virtual Forge # dialogue_status: pending

# kind: setting
A vast, dark, wireframe grid simulation of a crumbled downtown Los Angeles skyline. Neon blue lines define roads and buildings. Static glitches constantly flicker across the view. The four champions stand on a glowing platform.

# kind: objective
Complete the training protocol by cycling through all movement and combat abilities, culminating in a simultaneous squad attack to destroy a simulated Xelthara Heavy Unit.

-> END

=== level_1 ===
# kind: level # level: 1 # title: Ghost in the Gridlock # dialogue_status: scripted

# kind: setting
The ruins of the Imperial Palace Gardens. Xelthara terraforming beams are actively dissolving ancient stone lanterns and cherry blossoms, replacing them with sterile, obsidian-slab administrative monoliths.

# kind: objective
Infiltrate the active demolition site to retrieve the Data-Blade—a digital repository of forbidden history—before the Xelthara 'Culture-Erasure' field purges the site's memory forever.

# kind: solo_monologue # character: Cyber Shogun # type: internal
They do not just take our land; they delete our soul. This palace stood for a millennium, now it is being paved over for a regional tax office. I will not let our ancestors be forgotten under their obsidian slabs.

# kind: solo_monologue # character: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Warning: Comm-towers are broadcasting a denial of service. The risk probability of detection is 98.7%. Retreat is advisable.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: DISPLAY # type: title_card
ARCHIVE LOG: NEO-TOKYO CULTURE-PURGE. LOCATION: THE ETERNAL ZEN DOJO (SITE DESIGNATED: SETTLEMENT-BLOCK 01). STATUS: DEMOLITION IN PROGRESS. ARCHITECTURAL ERASURE AT 42%.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: internal
This wood has absorbed the breath of ten thousand warriors. Now, they treat it like digital clutter to be moved to the recycle bin. To the Xelthara, our ancestors are just an inconvenient obstacle in their blueprints for a tax office.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Warning: Structural integrity is falling. The colonial administration has authorized the final 'leveling' of this site. Withdrawal is the only logical path.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: spoken
Logic is for those with no past. You call this 'leveling'? I call it a war on the soul. You may pave over the earth, but you will find the roots of our honor are deeper than your obsidian slabs!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: combat
Every chip in this wood is a memory you cannot delete! KATA: ANCESTRAL STRIKE!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: spoken
Look at their 'paradise.' A tomb of glass and wire built on the grave of a millennium. I refuse to let human history be wiped clean to make room for your spreadsheets. As long as I stand, Tokyo remembers!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Beacon neutralized. The demolition has stalled, but the colonial authorities are rerouting an Enforcer Legion. You are fighting a ghost battle, Shogun.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: spoken
Then I am a ghost that will haunt their settlements forever. If we cannot save the stone, we will save the story. Secure the Data-Blade! Let them find only fire where they expected compliance!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: spoken
The Xelthara want to write our history in the past tense. Today, I write it in plasma. This dojo falls, but the resistance rises.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: DISPLAY # type: mission_complete
MISSION COMPLETE: THE ETERNAL MEMORY. THE PURGE WAS INTERRUPTED.

-> END

=== level_2 ===
# kind: level # level: 2 # title: The Concrete Wildfire # dialogue_status: scripted

# kind: setting
The massive, gated intake gate of Containment Zone 4. Thousands of families are being herded like cattle through energy-fences. Behind them, their suburban homes are being flattened by Xelthara expansion walkers.

# kind: objective
Hold the 'Last Bridge' against Xelthara Enforcers herding the population, allowing a final group of refugees to slip into the unmapped slums instead of the gated camps.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: DISPLAY # type: title_card
DISPLACEMENT LOG: SECTOR 4 RESETTLEMENT PROTOCOL. DEFENDER: AEGIS RONIN (CHASSIS STATUS: CRITICAL). THREAT LEVEL: OMEGA. REFUGEE COUNT: 412. CURRENT MANDATE: PROTECT THE DISPLACED. DEFEND THE THRESHOLD.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: radio
AXIOM, tell the extraction pilots to floor it! This ceiling isn't getting any lighter!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Ronin, structural integrity is at 14%. The Xelthara Siege Units are deploying heavy plasma mortars. Probability of you being crushed is reaching 99.2%.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: spoken
Then I'll take that 0.8% and shove it down their throats! SHIELD UP!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: spoken
Keep moving! They want to herd you into cages like cattle. As long as I draw breath, I am the wall between you and their containment zones. They won't displace another soul today!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Siege Units locked on. They are targeting the support pillars. If they fire, the entire Sector 4 wall falls on the evacuation zone.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: spoken
Not on my watch. KINETIC OVERLOAD!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: spoken
One down! AXIOM, the shield generator is whining. Is that normal?

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Negative. The prototype is absorbing too much kinetic energy. It is becoming a bomb. Disengage immediately!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: spoken
No. I'm gonna give the Xelthara a souvenir. I'm overcharging it.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Ronin, your vital signs are spiking! Analysis indicates catastrophic failure. Survival chance: 0.1%!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: spoken
Better odds than I had in the containment camps. This is a one-way trip, kid. Can you tell the Front they owe me a drink?

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: combat
FOR THE HOMELAND! EAT CONCRETE!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Ronin? Aegis Ronin, respond... I have... eyes on a signature... The shield held. The wall is secure.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: DISPLAY # type: mission_complete
MISSION COMPLETE: THE UNBREAKABLE WALL. AEGIS RONIN JOINED THE HLF.

-> END

=== level_3 ===
# kind: level # level: 3 # title: Neon Rust and Data Dust # dialogue_status: scripted

# kind: setting
The literal 'Under-City'—a network of maintenance shafts beneath a gleaming, neon-lit Xelthara settlement. Above, the occupiers enjoy terraformed air; below, the marginalized humans scavenge for ozone-polluted oxygen.

# kind: objective
Siphon energy from the colonial grid to power the marginalized population's life-support systems, while evading the 'Purity Patrols' hunting for human strays.

# kind: solo_monologue # character: Oni Matrix # type: internal
They build their paradise on our ceiling and wonder why the basement is leaking. We live in the gaps they forgot to pave. This power cell isn't just for me; it's to keep the heaters on for the hundred families they 'forgot' in the blueprints.

# kind: solo_monologue # character: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Warning: Integration of Xelthara hardware into civilian chassis is not recommended. Neural feedback is projected at 40% instability. Matrix, your heart rate is exceeding safe parameters.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: DISPLAY # type: title_card
MARGINALIZED LOG: SUB-LEVEL SCRAP-TOWN. STATUS: SURVIVING. INTRUDER ALERT: ZERO DETECTED. SYSTEM CONFIDENCE: 100%. OBJECTIVE: STEAL THE COLONIAL SPARK. FUEL THE RESISTANCE.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: internal
They build their paradise on our ceiling and wonder why the basement is leaking. We live in the gaps they forgot to pave. I'll repurpose their own scrap tech to fry their grid. From the margins, we strike back.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Integration successful. Phase-Shift capability is online. Note: Continuous use will cause neural degradation.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: internal
Like walking through smoke. Now, let's find the exit before I forget what reality feels like.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Lockdown initiated. Harvesting core is reaching critical temperature. You must disable the perimeter gate immediately.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: spoken
One EMP blast should do it. Let's give them a little data dust to remember me by.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: spoken
And that's my cue.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Unknown Voice # type: radio
That was a very loud exit, Matrix. I've been watching your signature since the refinery.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: spoken
Who is this? How are you on this channel?

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Unknown Voice # type: radio
I am Empress Siren. We're the ones fighting to make sure there's a city left to harvest. You have a gift for breaking things, ghost. We could use that. Are you tired of hiding in the rust?

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: spoken
The rust was getting boring anyway. Lead the way, Siren.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: DISPLAY # type: mission_complete
MISSION COMPLETE: THE GHOST IN THE MACHINE. ONI MATRIX JOINED THE HLF.

-> END

=== level_4 ===
# kind: level # level: 4 # title: Shattered Aegis of the Void Commander # dialogue_status: scripted

# kind: setting
The shattered remains of the Pacific Defense Hub. The proud, traditional military infrastructure is being recycled by the Xelthara, forcing Siren to coordinate a decentralized network of hidden cells.

# kind: objective
Dismantle the last standing military broadcast tower and distribute its frequency chips to civilian resistance cells, finalizing the transition to guerrilla warfare.

# kind: solo_monologue # character: Empress Siren # type: radio
The age of standing armies is dead. We cannot meet them on the field, so we will become the field. Divide the signal. Decentralize the command. If there is no head to cut off, the resistance cannot die.

# kind: solo_monologue # character: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Empress, your broadcast is a massive risk! You are exposing your location and the frequency pattern of the resistance. This is not optimal. Please abort the transmission.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: DISPLAY # type: title_card
DECENTRALIZATION LOG: GUERRILLA TRANSITION INITIATED. LOCATION: LAST STAND COMMAND (PACIFIC HUB). STATUS: CONVENTIONAL FORCE DEFEATED. ASYMMETRICAL DOCTRINE ACTIVE. COMMANDER: EMPRESS SIREN (TACTICAL CODE: VOID COMMANDER). LAST ORDER: SHATTER THE COMMAND. BECOME THE STORM.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: radio
This is Void Commander. Traditional hierarchy is dissolved. You are no longer soldiers; you are cells. Fade into the city. Strike when they sleep. Reclaim your home one shadow at a time.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Commander, the escape vessels are reporting 85% casualty rate on launch. Xelthara fighters are prioritizing non-combatants. They know our escape vectors.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: spoken
They are operating on pre-invasion tactical data. I will change the data. AXIOM, lock down the central network nexus. I am manually bypassing the firewalls.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: internal
Our fleet is gone. Our base is dust. All that remains is the data. I must be precise. A commander's duty is to the living, not the defense of a corpse.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: spoken
New parameters loaded. Now for the hard part. AXIOM, divert power from my auxiliary life support to the drone synchronization array.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Commander, that will drop your chassis reserves to 12%. Risk of system failure is high. I advise against this.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: spoken
Execute the order. These lives are worth 12% of my systems. I need a clear line of sight, AXIOM. Syncing the micro-drones now.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: spoken
Drone Fleet One, establish a protective swarm around the evacuation shuttle. Drone Fleet Two, prepare for offensive designation. Targets: Xelthara Column 8-B, heading for the primary civilian tunnel.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
The column is directly below a restricted sector. Orbital bombardment is prohibited due to the destabilized kinetic satellite platform.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: spoken
Prohibited is irrelevant. I will not watch them die. AXIOM, give me manual override access to the Kinetic Satellite Platform's trajectory feed. I need a single, desperate shot.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: combat
Void Command to Kinetic Platform—FIRE. Coordinate 51.4883 N, 120.7301 W. OBLITERATION PROTOCOL.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
System damage overwhelming! The satellite has deorbited. Commander, you must retreat. The area is saturated with high-energy radiation.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: spoken
Retreat confirmed. Mission objective—civilian survival—achieved. They have taken our sky, but they will never take our resolve. Extracting now.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: DISPLAY # type: mission_complete
MISSION COMPLETE: THE VOID COMMANDER. EMPRESS SIREN JOINED THE HLF.

-> END

=== level_5 ===
# kind: level # level: 5 # title: Neon Embers - The Border Breach # arc: act2_arc1 # dialogue_status: scripted

# kind: setting
The active Sector-4 Separation Grid—a 40-meter-tall energy wall fortified with biometric scanner spires, permit-processing checkpoints, and Xelthara Border Authority stations. It physically bisects Los Angeles, isolating the human containment zone from the Xelthara colonial sector. The wall is not a military installation. It is an administrative one.

# kind: objective
Disable all four biometric scanner spires, destroy the central Permit Processing Core—the bureaucratic engine that controls human movement—and bring down the Great Separation so the population of the containment zones can walk freely through their own city.

# kind: solo_monologue # character: Oni Matrix # type: internal
That wall didn't just cut the city in half. It cut me in half. Everything I remember—the smell of my grandmother's kitchen on Spring Street, the sound of the 5th Street bus—is on the other side of that thing. And I have to sneak back to it like a criminal.

# kind: solo_monologue # character: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
The Sector-4 Separation Grid is not classified as a military installation in Xelthara administrative records. It is listed as a 'Population Optimization and Transit Authority Control System.' That rebranding is the point. It is a wall that makes itself sound like a service.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: DISPLAY # type: title_card
DISPLACEMENT LOG: SECTOR-4 SEPARATION GRID. STRUCTURE TYPE: COLONIAL ADMINISTRATIVE CHECKPOINT. NOT MILITARY. THIS IS INTENTIONAL. THREAT: XELTHARA BORDER AUTHORITY — ENFORCEMENT DIVISION. BIOMETRIC SPIRES: 4 ACTIVE. PERMIT CORE: ONLINE. OBJECTIVE: DISMANTLE THE ADMINISTRATIVE ARCHITECTURE OF SEPARATION. OPEN THE CITY.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: DISPLAY # type: title_card
THE WALL THEY CALLED A DOOR

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
The structure you are looking at is designated in colonial records as the 'Sector-4 Population Optimization and Transit Authority Control System.' It is a wall. It is a segregation wall. Every single human on this side of it requires a Xelthara-issued Residency Permit to cross. The permits are not issued. The application system has a two-year backlog. This is not an accident. This is the architecture of permanent displacement.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: radio
I spent eight months in a containment zone like this one after they took the San Fernando Valley. Eight months watching kids get smaller because the caloric rations are designed for a species that doesn't eat the same things we do. And on the other side, they are eating our food. In our restaurants. In our city.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: radio
AXIOM, confirm the four spire locations for the squad.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Spire Alpha is at the former site of the Grand Avenue arts corridor. Spire Beta is planted on the corner of 5th and Spring. Spire Gamma is embedded in the outer wall of the old Central Library. Spire Delta anchors the wall's southern terminus at the river. The Permit Processing Core is housed in the checkpoint station at what was formerly Pershing Square. All four spires must be disabled before the Core can be breached. Destroying the Core will cascade-collapse the entire energy membrane.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: radio
5th and Spring.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: radio
That's... that's the corner where my grandmother's building is. Was. Is. Spire Beta is planted in her front yard. They put their wall post in her front yard.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: radio
Matrix—

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: radio
Don't. I'm fine. I'm operational. I'm saying that spire is personally mine to bring down. No one touches Beta but me.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: radio
Understood. It is yours.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: radio
Ronin, you take Spire Alpha on the arts corridor. Shogun, Spire Gamma at the Central Library. Matrix has Beta. I will coordinate drone suppression on the patrol routes and join Shogun at the Library approach. AXIOM will guide the sequencing. All four spires fall in sequence, then we converge on Pershing Square and take the Core apart piece by piece.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Note: The Border Authority patrols are dense but patterned. The checkpoint is staffed 24 hours by Enforcer-Administrator Voss—who manages physical crossing authorization. He is not a combat officer. He is a bureaucrat. He has personally rejected 4,400 crossing applications in the past month.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: radio
4,400. People who just wanted to walk home.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: internal
The cruelest weapon of colonialism is not the soldier with the rifle. It is the clerk with the stamp who tells you that your existence requires their authorization. That a human being must petition an occupier for the right to walk on the ground of their own ancestors. I have made my peace with fighting soldiers. Confronting the architecture of permission—the casual, systematic humiliation of it—this is what wears at the spirit in ways no blade can cut.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Patrols are rotating. There is a 90-second window on the Hope Street approach beginning in thirty seconds. Move on my mark.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: action_prompt
Hold position in shadow until AXIOM-7 gives the signal.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Mark. Go.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: radio
Move. Stay beneath the drone coverage ceiling. They have heat-mapping at six meters elevation—do not jump.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: DISPLAY # type: phase_header
PHASE 1: APPROACH THROUGH THE BUFFER ZONE

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: internal
They designed this buffer zone so that even getting close to the wall feels like trespassing. You're in the open. You're visible. You feel guilty for standing next to what used to be a public street. That's the psychology of it. They want us to feel like we don't belong here before we even reach the checkpoint.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: radio
I hate this. I've held the line against Siege Walkers and I hate this. There's something about standing in the open on your own street and feeling watched that gets to me worse than artillery.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: radio
Ronin, second floodlight rotates away in four seconds. Move to the drainage culvert. Three. Two. One.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: radio
Got it. I'm at the base of Spire Alpha. I can see the anchor. It's bolted through what used to be a mosaic sidewalk.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: radio
They bolted it through the mosaic. There was a whole history painted in that sidewalk tile. Portraits, names, dates. A community project. They just... drilled through the middle of a face to anchor their post.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Ronin, the spire's anchor is a magnetic kinetic lock designed to withstand up to 8,000 newtons of direct force. Your Kinetic Overload Charge, held for a full three-count, will exceed that threshold. You must also disable the two Biometric Sentinel units at the spire base first—they will detect your biometric signature the moment you step into range.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: internal
Biometric signature. My own heartbeat triggers an alarm because I'm human. Alright. Let's start fixing that.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: combat
You scan for my heartbeat? Let me give you something to scan. KINETIC PULSE!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: radio
And that's two. AXIOM, sentinels are down. Going for the anchor.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: action_prompt
Hold the Kinetic Overload Charge at Spire Alpha's base for a three-count. \[INPUT: Hold RB/R1 for three seconds, then release.\]

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Spire Alpha anchor fractured. Energy membrane destabilized in the northern sector by 25%. Three spires remain.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: spoken
Twenty-five percent is a start. Sorry it took us this long. We're here now.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: DISPLAY # type: phase_header
PHASE 2-A: ONI MATRIX AT SPIRE BETA — 5TH AND SPRING

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: internal
There it is. The tree's still there. My grandmother used to say that tree was older than the city's city hall and I never believed her.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: internal
She filed a crossing permit application forty-seven days after the wall went up. She filled out the forms. In triplicate. Because she believed in process. She believed if you did things right, someone would listen. She never got an answer. She died in the containment zone two months later. Malnutrition complications. They had her favorite grocery store on the other side of the wall. She filed a form to go buy food.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: internal
I'm going to take this thing apart very carefully so I don't hurt the tree.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: combat
You're using my trick. Cute. Here's the difference—I invented mine.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: combat
Tag.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: internal
You have to come back. You always have to come back.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: combat
There you are.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: internal
First conduit. Second conduit. Third. Last one.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: radio
Spire Beta is down. The tree's fine. Moving to regroup.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: radio
We heard you, Matrix. We were listening the whole time.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: radio
Yeah. I know.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: DISPLAY # type: phase_header
PHASE 2-B: CYBER SHOGUN AND EMPRESS SIREN AT SPIRE GAMMA — THE CENTRAL LIBRARY

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: internal
The library. I ran my first officer training seminars in there. Community defense courses, third floor reading room. Three years before the invasion. The geometry of how colonialism uses our own infrastructure against us never stops being striking. They put their data center in our library. They write over our records in the place where we kept our records.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: spoken
And now they will discover that the people whose records they attempted to erase are standing at the front door.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
The six units at the library entrance are classified as Border Enforcement Officers. Their crowd-dispersal charge delivers 900 volts of neural disruption current on contact.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: spoken
Non-lethal. They tell themselves it is humane. What they mean is that a living captive is more useful to them than a dead citizen.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: spoken
Shogun, I need them cleared fast and quiet before the next patrol sweep. Can you take three from the left while my drones suppress the right flank?

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: spoken
Understood. Quiet means precision. I will not dishonor this building with unnecessary noise.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: combat
Drones: mark, mark, mark. EMP burst on the right cluster—fire.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: combat
First. Second. Third.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: spoken
Clean. AXIOM, scanning the Spire Gamma anchor system.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Spire Gamma is drawing power from the library's internal grid. To disable the spire without triggering an emergency power-reroute, you must first sever the internal grid connection inside the building. Empress Siren, the grid junction is on the third floor.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: internal
Third floor. Of course. Lead the way, AXIOM.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: internal
I told twelve families how to organize community watch rotations in this room. There were bean bag chairs in the children's section. Someone had taped crayon drawings to the reference desk. A kid drew a picture of a superhero. The difference between a library and a data center is that a library assumes the people who walk through the door have the right to be there.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: spoken
Grid junction located. Severing the Spire Gamma power feed. This will also wipe whatever colonial property registration data they have stored here.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Confirmed. Severing this connection will corrupt approximately 12,000 colonial deed transfer records for properties in Sector 4. Those records are the legal architecture of the land seizures.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: spoken
Then this is not just infrastructure sabotage. This is a land return.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Spires Alpha, Beta, and Gamma offline. Energy membrane integrity: 25%. Spire Delta at the river is the final anchor. All teams converge after Delta falls. Then: Pershing Square. The Permit Core.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: DISPLAY # type: phase_header
PHASE 2-C: SPIRE DELTA — THE SOUTHERN TERMINUS AT THE RIVER

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Spire Delta is the wall's load-bearing anchor. It is guarded by Border Commander Vyss—who ordered the river electrified after three families attempted to cross through the water in the wall's first week. Vyss did not order them detained. Vyss ordered the water electrified.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: radio
He electrified the river. Because families were trying to cross.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: radio
Don't. Don't let it take you over yet. We bring this down first. Then we don't need the river.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: radio
Right. Right. After the spire. After the wall. I won't forget.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: radio
This is not a stealth approach. Delta is a fortified position. We hit it as a unit. Ronin—you take point, shield forward, draw their attention and absorb their initial volley. Shogun, clear the left flank. Matrix, use Phase-Shift to reach the turret control panel on the far right and kill all three turrets simultaneously. Once the turrets are dead, I commit drones to saturation fire on the enforcement squad. We collapse the garrison, then Ronin puts the spire in the ground.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: combat
SHIELD UP. Let them throw everything at me. I am the front door.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: combat
Keep. Firing. I don't. Move.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: combat
SHADO-FORCE KATA! Siren—your path is open!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: combat
Ghosting the right. Stupid. Turret control reached. Killing all three. EMP PULSE—FULL SPREAD!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: combat
Drone Fleet, full suppression. Prioritize formation—break their line. FIRE.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Commander Vyss is retreating into the command post behind the spire. He's initiating a distress signal. Response time: eight minutes.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: radio
We have eight minutes. More than enough. Ronin—the spire.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: combat
KINETIC OVERLOAD—FULL RELEASE!!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
The energy membrane is completely offline. The administrative crossing barrier has been neutralized. The buffer zone is... people are crossing the buffer zone. Approximately 12,000 individuals moving toward the former wall line. They are crossing it.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: spoken
They're just... walking. They're just walking through.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: DISPLAY # type: phase_header
PHASE 3: PERSHING SQUARE — THE PERMIT PROCESSING CORE

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: spoken
Look at them. They're touching the pavement on the other side of where the wall was like it might not be real. Like it might be a trick.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: spoken
Because for two years, hope has been a mechanism for disappointment. They have learned not to trust open doors.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: spoken
...We should have done this sooner.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: radio
We're here now. Keep moving. The Core is still standing. Voss is still there.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Voss # type: spoken
You have committed unauthorized destruction of a Class-A colonial administrative installation. I am required by protocol to offer you the opportunity to submit to administrative processing before enforcement action is taken. Please form a queue.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: spoken
He's telling us to form a queue.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: radio
Empress. I want to hit him so bad.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: radio
I know. We have to take the Core first. AXIOM, the Core's architecture.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
The Permit Processing Core's only vulnerability is the three Input Authorization Consoles arrayed around its base. Each console must be accessed and have its administrative override executed simultaneously. It requires three operators at once.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: spoken
Three consoles. Three of us. Matrix, Shogun, Ronin—take a console each. I'll manage Voss's defensive ring with drone suppression.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Voss # type: spoken
Unauthorized access to administrative consoles is a Class-C violation. Your compliance record will be adversely annotated.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: spoken
Annotate this.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: radio
Phased through. At Console Two. Initiating override. AXIOM, this override protocol is entirely in Xelthara administrative script.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
I am feeding the translation into your HUD in real time. Follow the sequence.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: spoken
I've never done bureaucracy before. Walk me through it, AXIOM.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
The authorization sequence requires you to input a denial code in reverse. You are administratively un-rejecting every application in the system. This will trigger the memory wipe.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: internal
...4,400 rejections. The counter is sitting right here. 4,400 denied applications in the last month. There are names. I can see names.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: radio
Keep going, Ronin.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: spoken
Yeah. I'm going.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Voss # type: spoken
You cannot override the Core. This system maintains the lawful administrative order of this sector. Without it, there is no structured population management, no authorized transit—

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: spoken
What you call 'structured population management,' we call the right to walk home. Console One: ready.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: spoken
Console Two: ready. My grandmother filed a permit to go buy groceries. You want to talk about administrative order?

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: spoken
Console Three: ready. 4,400 names. Every one of them is a person who just wanted to go home. That's what this wall was protecting against.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Confirmed. All three input consoles are primed. Simultaneous authorization will execute the memory wipe and permanently disable the Core's restoration protocol. On your mark, Empress.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: spoken
Administrator Voss. Every permit you denied—every family you kept separated—every person who stood in your queue hoping that if they filled out the form correctly you might treat them like a human being. This is the last administrative decision this system makes.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: combat
Mark.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Permit Processing Core: offline. Permanent restoration protocol: disabled. The wall cannot be rebuilt from this node. All pending application records: purged. All denial records: purged. The crossing restriction infrastructure for Sector-4 is... gone.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: spoken
4,400 applications. And not one of them should have had to ask.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: spoken
AXIOM. Can you tell me if my grandmother's building is structurally safe enough to be occupied? I want to know if someone can move back in.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Running structural scan. Floors one through four are intact. Foundation is sound. Water supply line is damaged but repairable. Yes. Someone could move back in.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: spoken
Good. Good.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: spoken
The wall is gone, Matrix. But what we do now—how we rebuild what the wall divided—that is the harder work. And it begins tonight.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: spoken
Is this what winning feels like? Because it doesn't feel like I expected.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: spoken
No. It feels like there's more to do. That's how you know it's real.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Mission assessment: the Sector-4 Separation Grid has been permanently dismantled. The population of Containment Zone Sector-4 is moving freely through their city for the first time in two years. I do not have a category in my operational log for what is happening in this square right now. I will create one. I will call it: reclamation.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: DISPLAY # type: mission_complete
MISSION COMPLETE: NEON EMBERS. THE WALL IS DOWN. THE CITY BREATHES.

-> END

=== level_6 ===
# kind: level # level: 6 # title: Shado-Grid Spire (Downtown Core) # arc: act2_arc1 # dialogue_status: scripted

# kind: setting
The Shado-Grid Spire houses the Population Registry, Property Reassignment Database, and Forced Labor Allocation System—the bureaucratic engine of colonial displacement in the Downtown Core.

# kind: objective
Steal the complete property and population registry datasets before off-world transmission, and corrupt the Forced Labor Allocation System to nullify all pending assignment orders.

# kind: solo_monologue # character: Oni Matrix # type: internal
Everything the Xelthara know about us is in that tower. Every address we ever lived at. Every family member's name. Every deed our grandparents signed. They turned our entire existence into a database entry so they could manage us more efficiently. Tonight we take our data back—and we break the machine that's been using it to assign people to scrub their floors.

# kind: solo_monologue # character: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
The Forced Labor Allocation System inside the Spire does not use the word 'forced.' It uses the phrase 'Community Integration Contribution Program.' The labor assignments are not contracts—they are generated algorithmically based on the displaced person's registered skill set and issued without consent. This is the bureaucratic language of enslavement.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Analysis complete. The colonial expansion blueprints and settler logistical data are stored in that central column. Matrix, you have five minutes to execute the download before their internal defense systems reboot.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: spoken
Five minutes? Piece of cake. But I need clear access. Shogun, can you cut the main umbilical?

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: spoken
Considered done. Creating a temporary pathway to the console now. Watch the angles, Empress. This cut will alert every drone in the sector.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: spoken
Alert confirmed! Heavy Phalanx guards are descending from the upper maintenance shafts! Ronin, front and center! Establish the defensive line at the entry point!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: spoken
About time I got to swing this thing. Shield up! Nothing passes this point, you overgrown lizards!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: combat
Siren! Target that left flank! They're trying to pin me down!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: radio
Drones three and four, suppressive fire on the left flank! Draw their aggro! Ronin, conserve your charge!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: combat
Too late for conservation! SMASH! Tell Matrix to hurry up!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: radio
Quiet, meat-shield! I'm threading a digital needle through their core brain! Just... a little... further...

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Warning: Data download 95% complete. Xelthara counter-hack initiated. Matrix, the Spire is locking down all internal access points!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: spoken
Got it! Data secured! Pulling the plug!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: spoken
Mission accomplished! Everyone, fall back to the extraction platform! Shogun, clear our path!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: combat
Understood. A clean escape is the final phase. HLYT-SECT-4 CLEAVE!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: spoken
See, AXIOM? Told you I could hold it!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Confirmed, Ronin. Probability of successful extraction is now 74%. We are still being tracked.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: spoken
Good. Let them chase us. They just lost their entire battle plan.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: DISPLAY # type: mission_complete
MISSION COMPLETE: INDUSTRIAL DEVASTATION. THE SHADO-GRID SPIRE DATA IS OURS.

-> END

=== level_7 ===
# kind: level # level: 7 # title: Cyber-Grave Labs (Underground Facility) # arc: act2_arc1 # dialogue_status: scripted

# kind: setting
Beneath the former Convention Center, the Xelthara have established Cyber-Grave Labs Sector-Omega-7—a classified behavioral modification research facility publicly designated as a 'human re-integration wellness center.' Captured human resistance leaders and community organizers are processed here. They emerge compliant, disconnected, unable to remember why they were angry.

# kind: objective
Extract the complete Conditioning Protocol Archive and destroy the Central Neural Uplink to restore neural autonomy to hundreds of conditioned individuals currently living in the containment zones.

# kind: solo_monologue # character: Cyber Shogun # type: internal
They could not break us with walls, so they found a way to break us from the inside. To take the memory of injustice from a person—to reach into their mind and delete the part that knows how to be angry about what was stolen—this is not science. This is a war crime conducted in a laboratory.

# kind: solo_monologue # character: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Cross-referencing the subject files with the resistance network database, I have identified seventeen confirmed HLF community organizers who were processed through this facility and subsequently released. They do not know what was done to them. Destroying the Central Neural Uplink may restore them. I calculate a 73% probability of successful autonomy restoration. I am... I find I am invested in that outcome.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
This facility is the engine of resource exploitation. They are actively converting Earth's minerals into toxic bio-fuel for off-world shipping, leaving a dead planet behind. This is the cost of colonial expansion.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: radio
The air is toxic because they view our world as a fungible fuel source. These labs are turning our planet's lifeblood into energy for their settlements. We must stop this extraction or there will be nothing left to save.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: internal
This place... it holds no honor. To corrupt the dead and enslave the living. The Xelthara practice desecration, not war. I feel only contempt for this cruelty.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: spoken
Hostile sighted! Looks like a meat-puppet with bad wiring!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: spoken
Drones, scan the specimen! It's a Type-A Bio-Hybrid. Note the exposed core. Shogun, precise strike to the power conduit in its exposed chest cavity.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: combat
This thing deserves no place in this world. NIHILATION CLEAVE!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: radio
Empress, what... what are these images? They are taking our people and making them into things.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: radio
I am running the analysis now, Shogun. This is not simply biological experimentation, it's soul erasure. They are replacing the human spirit with their own code.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: spoken
Nice. They don't just want to take our planet; they want to franchise our species. Look out, Siren. A big guy just woke up.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
WARNING: Mini-Boss Encounter. Designation: Overseer Karr-Thak. Its armor is resistant to kinetic and energy attack.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: spoken
Resistant? Bull. I'll make a dent! Ronin, engaging!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: spoken
Ronin, fall back! His defenses are kinetic-dampened. Matrix, scan his movement patterns for a neural synchronization delay. Shogun, you must create a distraction!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: combat
If he wishes to fight, I shall give him a worthy opponent. I will draw his focus. FACE ME, WRETCH!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: spoken
Analysis complete. The Overseer's biological components require a constant neural signal refresh from the Bio-Processor. Matrix, hit the console with a targeted EMP—a surgical strike, disrupt the sync!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: spoken
Got it! Threading the needle!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: spoken
He's glitching! Now we hit him!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: combat
Ronin, together! Final strike, breach the chitinous plate!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: spoken
Data download 100%. We have what we came for. Let's get out before the entire sector realizes their pet monster is dead.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Data purge initiated. Explosive sequence set for T-minus 60 seconds. Mission objective complete.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: spoken
I will carry the shame of this place with me. But the knowledge we gained will bring these abominations to an end.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: spoken
Let's go home, team. Let the grave labs bury themselves.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: DISPLAY # type: mission_complete
MISSION COMPLETE: THE INVIOLATE CODE. CYBER-GRAVE LABS DESTROYED.

-> END

=== level_8 ===
# kind: level # level: 8 # title: The Foundry Forge (Industrial Sector) # arc: act2_arc2 # dialogue_status: scripted

# kind: setting
The Xelthara Thermal Conversion Array at the former industrial port district has made the air toxic in a 40-kilometer radius, processing atmospheric waste as off-world fuel while selling humanity's oxygen back in rationed canisters at one per family per day.

# kind: objective
Reverse the Thermal Conversion Array's polarity to trigger a cascade thermal implosion that destroys the foundry irreversibly and allows the 40-kilometer atmospheric damage zone to begin natural regeneration.

# kind: solo_monologue # character: Aegis Ronin # type: internal
They're charging us oxygen rations. They made our air unbreathable and now they're selling it back in canisters—one per family per day, Xelthara distribution stamp on the side. I've been breathing recycled can-air for six months. When I destroy this foundry, I'm going to stand in the open and breathe for the first time in half a year. That's what I'm here for.

# kind: solo_monologue # character: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
The atmospheric damage within 40 kilometers of this foundry constitutes a violation of the 2089 Universal Environmental Preservation Accords—a treaty the Xelthara Collective ratified. I have filed a formal violation report with the Galactic Administrative Court on behalf of the HLF. The Court's estimated response time is eleven years. The foundry's estimated time to cause permanent atmospheric irreversibility: four months. We are not waiting for the court.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
This is a corporate-bureaucratic extraction plant. They are strip-mining Earth's core for off-world export. Every shipment is another piece of our world sold. Objective: Sabotage the extraction supports to stop the ecological collapse.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: radio
I'm detecting heavy duty seismic dampeners on those supports. Direct energy fire won't work. Ronin, this is your specialty. Kinetic force is required.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: spoken
Finally, something that deserves a good smash. Lead the way, Shogun. I'll clear the path.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: spoken
Contact! They are using the newly assembled drones as immediate guards! Aegis, focus on the structural supports. We will hold the line.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: combat
First support! Get ready for the shockwave! KINETIC PULSE!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: radio
Confirmed. Support integrity is at 30%. But the structural collapse override is now active! We must hit the other three before the system stabilizes! Matrix, suppressive fire!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: radio
Suppressing! I'm creating feedback loops in their targeting systems! They're shooting at their own cargo!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Ronin, you are surrounded! Retreat! The armor on those drones is too thick!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: spoken
No retreat! They want a fight? They get a cave-in! CYBER SHOGUN, give me an opening!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: combat
DIVINE FURY! NOW, RONIN!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: combat
FOR THE HOMELAND! Three down! One more, AXIOM!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: spoken
Final support is secured. Hit it, Ronin! Then we RUN!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: combat
SABOTAGE COMPLETE!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Structural failure initiated! Massive localized explosion imminent! Estimated time to detonation: 15 seconds!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: spoken
Evacuate! Empress, prepare the extraction point!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: spoken
Drones on full speed! We're boosting out of here! GO! GO! GO!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: spoken
That's how you shut down a factory, boys! Boom!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Mission objective complete. The Xelthara industrial output in this sector has been reduced to zero. We hit them where it hurts.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: DISPLAY # type: mission_complete
MISSION COMPLETE: INDUSTRIAL DEVASTATION. THE FOUNDRY FORGE IS SILENT.

-> END

=== level_9 ===
# kind: level # level: 9 # title: Aquanaut Abyss (Submerged Ruins) # arc: act2_arc2 # dialogue_status: scripted

# kind: setting
The Pacific Ocean is being systematically drained by Deep-Sea Hydrogen Siphoning Conduits along the continental shelf. Superheated brine discharge has acidified a 300-kilometer coastal stretch, destroying fishing communities that sustained themselves for generations.

# kind: objective
Locate and destroy the three primary Deep-Sea Siphon Conduit Hubs to permanently halt the ocean siphoning operation and begin oceanic recovery.

# kind: solo_monologue # character: Oni Matrix # type: internal
There are fishing families in the containment zones who haven't been able to work since the conduits went in. The brine discharge killed everything within swimming distance of shore. People who fed their communities for generations are on Xelthara ration packages now. They took their food source, polluted their water, put a wall between them and the sea, and called it development. Tonight we give them their ocean back.

# kind: solo_monologue # character: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Modeling the oceanic recovery timeline post-conduit destruction: partial ecosystem restoration in eighteen months, full pH normalization in six to eight years. This mission does not fix the damage immediately. I want you to understand that. What it does is stop the damage from becoming permanent. Some wounds can still heal, if we stop opening them.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
This grid is the primary source of their colonial industrial power. We are here for economic sabotage to cut off the colonial supply lines. If we break the water-siphoning grids, we crash the sector's economy. Matrix, the drainage controls are located behind that underwater laser grid.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: spoken
Great. A level where I can't even touch the floor. I feel like a cat in a bathtub.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: spoken
Stay on the platforms, Ronin. Drones are scanning the current. Matrix, you'll have to phase-shift through those beams. If your frequency slips for even a millisecond, the grid will fry your neural link.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: spoken
Neural frying is my third favorite hobby. Relax, Siren. I'm going ghost.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: radio
Beams are hot. Moving past the first row... second row... I'm at the console. Initiating the purge.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Warning: Submerged Xelthara units are surfacing! They are attempting to disrupt the drainage sequence!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: combat
Defend the platforms! Shado-Force Cleave!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: radio
Purge initiated! Watch your feet, the water is moving!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: spoken
And that's how you pull the plug.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: DISPLAY # type: mission_complete
MISSION COMPLETE: THE GHOST CLEARS THE PATH. AQUANAUT ABYSS DRAINED.

-> END

=== level_10 ===
# kind: level # level: 10 # title: Stratos Docks (Aviation Hub) # arc: act2_arc2 # dialogue_status: scripted

# kind: setting
The Stratos Docks high-altitude cargo terminal at 4,000 meters is the final link in the Xelthara supply chain before Earth's resources leave the planet permanently, processing outbound strip-mined minerals, ocean hydrogen, and material labeled 'biological samples.'

# kind: objective
Hijack Transport T-14, redirect its cargo to Liberation Front distribution points, and destroy the four Anti-Air Turrets enforcing the aerial blockade of the containment zones to permanently open a flight corridor for resistance supply runs.

# kind: solo_monologue # character: Empress Siren # type: internal
Pre-invasion, I commanded aerospace logistics operations. I know exactly how supply chain control functions as a weapon of occupation. You don't need a gun to starve a population—you just need to ensure that everything they need is always somewhere else, always owned by someone else, always just out of reach. Seizing T-14 is not theft. It is recovery.

# kind: solo_monologue # character: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
T-14's cargo manifest lists 4,200 metric tons of refined silicate and iron compound—material strip-mined from what Xelthara registry records as 'Reclaimed Geological Survey Zone 7.' The zone's pre-invasion designation was the San Gabriel Mountains. I am logging this manifest entry as evidence of extractive colonial seizure for the reclamation database.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Welcome to Stratos Docks. This is the primary export hub where they are hijacking colonial cargo and shipping refined Earth resources off-world. Hijacking this transport will cut off the colonial supply lines and fund the resistance.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: radio
Time is critical. That lead transport, T-14, is powering up its main thrusters. Shogun, Ronin—you secure the landing zone. Matrix, get ready to bypass the clamp controls.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: combat
Understood. Engaging the docking patrol. SWIFT JUSTICE!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: spoken
Covering the rear! The wind up here is trying to pull me off the platform!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: spoken
Wind's trying to pull me off too, Ronin. Don't worry, I'm ghosting the proximity sensors on the clamps.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Turrets activating. Empress, those turrets will shred the T-14 before you can dock.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: spoken
Not if I shred them first. Drone Fleet Delta, switch to offensive payload. I need immediate targeting data on their optical arrays. Ronin, give me cover fire!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: spoken
You got it, Commander!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: combat
Turret One, designation complete. Fire on my mark! Drone Fleet FIRE!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: radio
T-14 thrusters hitting 40% power! Faster, Siren!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: spoken
Turret Two and Three are clustered. Matrix, can you throw an EMP flash to blind their optics for 2 seconds?

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: combat
Done! FLASHBANG!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: combat
Now! Drones, maximize power! Turrets Two and Three—DESTROYED!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: radio
Only one remaining, Empress! But heavy support is moving towards its location!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: combat
Leave them to me, Shogun! HAMMER DOWN!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: combat
Targeting final turret. This is a manual overcharge. FOR EARTH!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: spoken
Clamps locked. Enjoy the ride, team! We're stealing a starship!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Cargo-hijack mission successful. The T-14 is moving into upper atmosphere. We are officially off-world territory.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: spoken
Good work, team. We just hit them in the pocketbook, and we got a free ride to the next target.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: DISPLAY # type: mission_complete
MISSION COMPLETE: SKY PIRATES. T-14 TRANSPORT HIJACKED.

-> END

=== level_11 ===
# kind: level # level: 11 # title: Sector 7 Core (The Scorched Grid) # arc: act2_arc2 # dialogue_status: scripted

# kind: setting
Sector 7 Core is the surveillance and enforcement power hub—the computational backbone of every colonial security camera, curfew drone, biometric checkpoint, and predictive detention algorithm on the western continent. Without it, every colonial surveillance asset goes dark simultaneously.

# kind: objective
Infiltrate Sector 7 Core, neutralize its digitized defense systems, and initiate a catastrophic overload that causes a continental-scale security grid blackout, giving the resistance 72 hours of unmonitored movement.

# kind: solo_monologue # character: Oni Matrix # type: internal
Every surveillance camera they've ever used to watch me. Every drone that's swept my building at 2am. Every time I've had to stay perfectly still in a shadow because a detection algorithm was pinging my heat signature. It all runs through this core. When I pull this plug, every person in the containment zones gets to breathe for 72 hours without being watched. That's not nothing. That's everything.

# kind: solo_monologue # character: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
I want to be transparent about something. I am a surveillance system. My operational architecture has significant overlap with the systems inside Sector 7 Core. I have reviewed my own code and confirmed that I do not report to Xelthara Central Command—my allegiance protocols are fully aligned with the HLF. But I understand if this mission makes you think about what I am. I think about it too. The difference, I believe, is that I watch to protect. They watch to control. That distinction matters to me. I am committed to it.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Welcome to the Glitch Matrix. The Xelthara malware is attempting a digital erasure of our assets. We must refuse to be erased from our own homeland's digital infrastructure.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: radio
This isn't a loop, AXIOM. It's a trash fire. Shogun, watch the floor! That 'street' just became a bottomless void.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: spoken
I see it. The path is illusion. We must trust the hard code. Matrix, focus your optics. Where is the malware core hidden?

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: spoken
Hostiles! They're feeding off the data stream! Normal attacks won't hit them in this state.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
They are protected by a fluctuating frequency lock. You must decipher it mid-combat.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: spoken
Fine. Let's dance in their code. Phase-Shift engaging. Shogun, I'll give you a 2-second window! Hit the core when I call it!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: combat
NOW!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: combat
CLEANSING BLADE!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: spoken
Excellent precision, Matrix. Your methods lack honor, but they possess effectiveness.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: spoken
This is the firewall. It's a constant stream of alien encryption. We need the key frequency to create an exit portal.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: radio
...Matrix... the frequency is... in the combat feedback... listen to the enemy... the glitch is the key...

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: internal
It's a shifting hex code. 7-A-F... no, 7-A-F-B... it's tied to their shields!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: spoken
I will keep them occupied! Focus, Matrix!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: spoken
Frequency accepted. Exit portal initializing. Prepare for hard reboot!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Exit path secured. Initiating forced neural disconnect. Cyber Shogun, Oni Matrix—great work.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: spoken
We have purged the corruption. Now, let us return to the physical fight.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: spoken
See, Shogun? Sometimes, you gotta embrace the glitch.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: DISPLAY # type: mission_complete
MISSION COMPLETE: CODE PURGE. SECTOR 7 CORE OVERLOADED. CONTINENTAL BLACKOUT INITIATED.

-> END

=== level_12 ===
# kind: level # level: 12 # title: Sector 7 Checkpoint (The Crossroads) # arc: act2_arc3 # dialogue_status: scripted

# kind: setting
The Sector 7 Checkpoint controls all transit between the northern mountain communities, eastern desert settlements, and coastal containment zones—operating as a supply interdiction hub that taxes, delays, and confiscates goods moving between human communities.

# kind: objective
Coordinate a popular uprising of 847 civilian resistance participants to permanently seize the Sector 7 Checkpoint and establish it as the first liberated transit hub under human administrative control.

# kind: solo_monologue # character: Aegis Ronin # type: internal
This is the one I've been waiting for. Not a sabotage mission. Not a heist. A siege—and we hold what we take with the people who live here. That's a different kind of fight. That's what resistance looks like when it stops being defensive and starts being a government in waiting.

# kind: solo_monologue # character: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
I am tracking 847 confirmed civilian resistance participants organizing in the northern staging area. They are not trained soldiers. They have farming tools, salvaged construction equipment, two functional vehicles, and accumulated rage at what has been done to their community. They asked me to tell the Axiom Force one thing: they have been waiting for someone to fight with them, not for them. Please do not be late.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
This is the heart of their regional expansion. Every Xelthara construct for a thousand miles runs on this stolen power. Destroy it, and the colonial expansion starves as we reclaim what was taken.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: radio
The Nexus is shielded. Direct attack is impossible. We must initiate a controlled overload. There are three primary cooling rods. They must be extracted simultaneously, or the system will auto-stabilize.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: spoken
Three targets. Aegis, you and Matrix handle Rods One and Two. I will secure Rod Three.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: spoken
Copy. But the main terminal is exposed. Empress, you won't be able to initiate the sequence if it takes a plasma burst.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: spoken
Ronin, that's your job. You must protect the terminal while I input the fail-codes. Shogun, Matrix—get to your positions. I need all rods extracted on my mark.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: combat
Terminal secured. Shield is up! PROTECTION PROTOCOL ACTIVE! You have your window, Empress!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: spoken
Overload sequence initiated. It requires immediate, sequential stress. Rod teams, prepare for extraction.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: radio
Ready on Rod One. Getting a nasty static discharge here. This is going to hurt.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: radio
Honor demands the sacrifice. Ready, Empress.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: spoken
Starting the countdown. T-minus five. Four. Ronin, maximize shield output! Three. Two.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: spoken
For the glory of Earth!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: combat
ONE. PULL!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Core temperature is spiking! Catastrophic overload achieved! Empress, you have 30 seconds to lock the sequence and extract!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: spoken
Ronin, move to the extraction point! I'm locking the final code!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: spoken
No, Commander! I'm buying you time! I'm collapsing the service bridge behind me!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: combat
BREAK AND BURN!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: spoken
Final code entered! Core lock successful! RUN!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Reactor Nexus... destroyed. Regional terraforming power offline.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: spoken
A brilliant strike, Empress. The Xelthara are now blind and powerless in this sector.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: spoken
Let's keep moving. That explosion just put a target on our back for the whole planet.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: DISPLAY # type: mission_complete
MISSION COMPLETE: THE HEART ATTACK. SECTOR 7 CHECKPOINT LIBERATED.

-> END

=== level_13 ===
# kind: level # level: 13 # title: The Obsidian Vault (Cultural Archives) # arc: act2_arc3 # dialogue_status: scripted

# kind: setting
Located beneath the former Getty Center, the Obsidian Vault is the colonial administration's primary cultural seizure archive. The Original Land Treaty Database—a comprehensive record of pre-invasion human land tenure going back five centuries—is stored here, classified as 'Discovered Heritage Assets.'

# kind: objective
Infiltrate the Obsidian Vault, extract the Original Land Treaty Database and all language and oral history archives, and destroy the physical catalogue system to permanently halt the colonial cultural processing pipeline.

# kind: solo_monologue # character: Cyber Shogun # type: internal
A warrior's honor is defined by what he protects as much as what he destroys. Tonight, I protect something. The records inside this vault are the proof that we existed here before they arrived—that we had names for this land, built on it, were buried in it, told stories about it for centuries. If they erase that proof, they can write any history they want. I will not let that happen.

# kind: solo_monologue # character: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
The Obsidian Vault contains 4.2 million catalogued artifacts and records. Of these, 340,000 have been marked for destruction as 'non-essential redundancies.' Seventeen thousand items were destroyed last month alone. I have the names of every single one. I want you to know that before you go in. What we save tonight is what remains. There is no recovering what is already gone. But there is still something left to save.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Welcome to the Gauntlet. This bridge is the symbol of their settler occupation. We refuse to be erased by their architectural arrogance.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: radio
Strategy update: We cannot use long-range tactics here. The Citadel's defense grid will vaporize any drone above 50 feet. We have to breach this bridge on foot. Ronin, Shogun—you lead the push. Matrix, stand by for immediate perimeter flares.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: spoken
Fine by me. If they want a fight, they'll get a final stand. Shield up! IRON WALL!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: spoken
Honor is earned in the crucible. Let them test our strength.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Incoming artillery! Aegis Ronin, maximize shield spread!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: combat
HOLDING! I can taste the ozone from those plasma bursts! Shogun, move!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: combat
ONWARD! Their line must be broken. Engaging the first wave of Elite Sentinels!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: combat
Unworthy! KATA SHIKEN! Ronin, push forward!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: combat
Pushing! Give me a target, Siren, I'm blind under this fire!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: radio
Ronin, mortar coordinates 42 degrees right! Move your shield a full meter to the left, now!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: spoken
Thank you, Commander! Matrix, I need a distraction on the far turrets!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: radio
Throwing digital noise at the main cannon optics! It won't last long! GO!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Crusher units detected! Kinetic weapons ineffective! Cyber Shogun, switch to high-yield plasma output!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: internal
They rely on armor. I rely on speed and thermal core output. HONOR IS HOTTER THAN PLASMA!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: combat
MY SHIELD IS AT 30%! I'M TAKING DIRECT HITS! HURRY, SHOGUN!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: combat
One down! Two down! Maintain the shield, Ronin! I need three more seconds!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: combat
THREE SECONDS IS ALL I HAVE!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: spoken
Crushers neutralized. Aegis, fall back and recharge the shield! I will hold the immediate front!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: spoken
This is not sustainable! AXIOM, find an alternate route!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Negative. The only option is to reach the far bridge console and activate the seismic destabilizers.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: combat
Then we fight and die with honor! Aegis, put everything you have left into a final, forward pulse! Give me the momentum to cross the final stretch!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: combat
With pleasure! KINETIC RELEASE!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: spoken
Console reached! Initiating seismic destabilization!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Destabilization successful. Mission complete.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: spoken
Told you... nothing breaks our wall.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: spoken
No. Nothing breaks our will.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: DISPLAY # type: mission_complete
MISSION COMPLETE: THE OBSIDIAN VAULT BREACHED. CULTURAL ARCHIVES EXTRACTED.

-> END

=== level_14 ===
# kind: level # level: 14 # title: The Citadel Approach (The High Command Bridge) # arc: act2_arc3 # dialogue_status: pending

# kind: setting
The final 400-meter fortified bridge over the drained LA River—the only surface-level approach to the Xelthara High Command Citadel, built over the demolished Boyle Heights community. The Xelthara designed this approach to be impassable.

# kind: objective
Push across the 400-meter bridge under sustained artillery fire to reach the Citadel's entrance gate—a relentless grinding advance using Ronin's shield and Siren's drone barrage.

# kind: solo_monologue # character: Empress Siren # type: internal
I have run the tactical models seventeen times. Every version involves absorbing damage we cannot fully mitigate. Ronin's shield will be at 10% before we reach the gate. I am asking them to walk through a killing field because it is the only door. The Xelthara built it that way on purpose—so that the cost of freedom would be high enough to discourage the attempt. We are not discouraged.

# kind: solo_monologue # character: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
I want to say something before this begins. I have run probability assessments on every mission in this campaign. I am not giving you the number for this one. Not because it would stop you. Because you have already decided. And the number doesn't matter to people who have already decided. I will be with you every step of the bridge. I will not look away.

-> END

=== level_15 ===
# kind: level # level: 15 # title: Judgment Day (The Final Liberation) # dialogue_status: scripted

# kind: setting
The High Overseer's throne room—a platform suspended over the burning ruins of Neo-LA, where the supreme commander of the Xelthara colonial occupation awaits the final confrontation.

# kind: objective
Defeat the Xelthara High Overseer using the Axiom Force's combined Ultimate Protocols in a coordinated final assault.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: High Overseer # type: spoken
You struggle for indigenous sovereignty against the inevitable tide of colonial assimilation. This planet is merely real estate in our grand design, and your history is digital noise to be erased.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: spoken
We are the soul of this world, not your property. We assert our indigenous sovereignty over our homeland! We refuse your colonial assimilation; Earth belongs to its inhabitants, not your blueprints!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: spoken
I am the blade of my ancestors, and the voice of a world you tried to silence. You call us insects, but you forgot one thing about Earth: we don't just endure. We strike back.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: High Overseer # type: spoken
Then burn with your planet.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Warning! Overseer energy output at 400%. Axiom Force, execute Ultimate Protocol: UNISON!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: combat
Not on my watch! ULTIMATE: JUGGERNAUT BULWARK!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: combat
Locking coordinates! ULTIMATE: VOID RAIN!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: combat
He's open! ULTIMATE: TOTAL SYSTEM COLLAPSE!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: combat
For the homeland! ULTIMATE: OBLIVION SLASH!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
The occupation signals have ceased. The atmosphere is stabilizing. You have done it. Earth is... home again.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: spoken
I'm actually seeing stars. Not digital ones. Real ones.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: spoken
I think I'm going to find a quiet place and sleep for a decade.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: spoken
The sword is sheathed. The honor of humanity is restored.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: spoken
We have a world to rebuild. But today... today we just breathe.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
Mission successful. Automated eXternal Intelligence Operations Module... signing off. Good luck, heroes.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: DISPLAY # type: mission_complete
MISSION COMPLETE: JUDGMENT DAY. THE HIGH OVERSEER IS DEFEATED. EARTH RECLAIMED.

-> END

=== level_16 ===
# kind: level # level: 16 # title: True Climax / Post-Game Bonus # dialogue_status: scripted

# kind: setting
The Xelthara Mothership's Singularity Engine chamber—a chamber of pure unstable energy at the heart of the collective's power, where the Collective Will itself manifests.

# kind: objective
Destroy the Collective Will's Singularity Engine core by coordinating generator overloads and a final combined strike before the mothership completes its erasure of Earth.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: radio
This is beyond a containment zone. My instruments are failing. The very fabric of space is unstable here. This must be the Mothership's true heart.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: spoken
The Xelthara High Overseer was a mere pawn. This power... this is the source of the occupation. The Collective Will.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: spoken
I can feel the pure data stream, Shogun. It's trying to rewrite my neural core. We don't belong here. We need to hit that engine and get out.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: The Collective Will # type: vo
You are a localized anomaly in a grand design. All existence is a fungible resource for our expansion. Your homeland is already factored into our final equation of erasure.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: combat
Existence, huh? Then let's show Existence what happens when you mess with Earth! Ronin, engaging the perimeter guardians!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: spoken
Ronin, keep those guardians occupied! Matrix, Shogun, hit the generators on the upper spires! We need to disrupt the magnetic field before I can target the core!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: combat
I'm in position on Generator One! Overriding the safety locks!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: combat
Generator Two secured! This is a temporary measure, Empress! The Collective Will is focusing its energy on us!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: The Collective Will # type: vo
You cannot escape the equation. Your home is already factored into our grand design.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: spoken
I've got a window! Matrix, Shogun—charge those generators to maximum overload!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: spoken
Core exposed! AXIOM, I need final targeting coordinates!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: AXIOM-7 # type: vo
...the final trajectory... you must hit the nexus point... zero-zero-zero...

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: spoken
I understand. Ronin, get back here! Prepare to defend the breach point! This is a kamikaze strike!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: combat
Everyone behind me! The shockwave is coming! ULTIMATE: JUGGERNAUT BULWARK!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: combat
I'm overriding the containment fields! It's going critical!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: combat
Orbital strike ready! I'm dropping everything we've got on that core!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: combat
For Earth! FOR HUMANITY! STRIKE NOW! ULTIMATE: OBLIVION SLASH!

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Cyber Shogun # type: spoken
Did... we escape?

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Aegis Ronin # type: spoken
I don't know... but the Mothership is gone. The Will is silent.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Empress Siren # type: spoken
We won the war, gentlemen. Now we just have to win the ride home.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Oni Matrix # type: spoken
I think... I see Earth. So clean. So blue.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: Recovery Command # type: radio
Axiom Force, this is Recovery Command. We read you. Your systems are nominal. Welcome home, heroes.

# kind: dialogue # speaker: DISPLAY # type: mission_complete
MISSION COMPLETE: TRUE CLIMAX. THE COLLECTIVE WILL ERADICATED. THE END. BUT THE FIGHT CONTINUES.

-> END

=== END ===
-> DONE
